      "message": "Even for included sample certs you don\u0027t need that. If you look at the code, it is used  by keystone-manage tool which is not part of the keystone server, and it is  an external utility for dev/test. You don\u0027t want to include the configuration for the external utility in keystone.conf\n\nIn other words,  once you have generated the self signed certs, remove cert_key ,key_size from the configuration file  It will work.  Ideally keystone-mange should take the key size as command line arg.\n\nSince keystone has this, other projects such as devstack, tripleo have this in their configuration.",
